# Entry point sourced into the global Kconfig tree (via zephyr/module.yml).

menuconfig API_VALIDATION
	bool "Shared validation and error codes for the web API"
	help
	  The contract's error table as code: every rejection gets its code, its
	  HTTP status, its retryable flag, its field paths and its JSON shape
	  from one place, so route handlers cannot drift apart. Also carries the
	  strict parsers the contract needs for addresses and opaque ids. No
	  dynamic allocation and no networking dependency. See
	  include/api_validation/api_validation.h.

if API_VALIDATION

config API_VALIDATION_MAX_FIELDS
	int "Field-level errors carried in one rejection"
	default 6
	range 1 32
	help
	  Each entry costs a path buffer, and an error is meant to live in a
	  request context rather than on a deep stack, so this is deliberately
	  small. Overflow is not silent: the rejection is marked truncated so a
	  client knows the list is partial. Six covers every form in the first
	  version with room to spare.

endif # API_VALIDATION
